window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b><i>The Pride of Alphas Complete Collection: Books 1-3</i></b></p> <p><b><i>Hunting Ember</i></b></p> <p>Ember Brady would never describe herself as stubborn. She's a pastry chef. Doesn't that make her patient by definition? Who cares if she's set in her ways? So what if she doesn't relent? It's called passion and determination. She wants to open her own bakery, and the baking competition is her ticket to her dream job. She would die to win. That's just a figure of speech, though.</p> <p>Lion-shifter Kai Mason is proud of his family's security business. They're in charge of all things security at F&amp;D Network, from actors to infuriating reality TV competitors. The studio is his domain and his to protect. If only the stubborn baker with a death wish would just let him save her. Doesn't she understand that she's his mate?</p> <p>When the baking competition comes under attack, the intense lion and his stubborn mate will have to find a compromise. Too bad both of them are out of practice. Crashing equipment, death threats, and vicious attacks can't stop the course of true love - or can they?</p> <p><b><i>Chasing Sparx</i></b></p> <p>Sparx Brady is sick of playing the same role. She’s been on the same soap opera since she was 14. She needs change and adventure. When the role of a lifetime comes around, she’s determined to be cast. She quits her job and heads to the mountains for a week-long survivalist course. She’s a stubborn Brady woman; she’s got this.</p> <p>Tiger-shifter Dash Jones doesn’t talk. He can, but he prefers quiet contemplation on his mountain. The only time he interacts is when he’s teaching a survivalist course. It’s a fun, easy enough gig. But when a shiny actress in heels drives up to his mountain, he tries to chase the chatty woman away. He doesn’t want a mate. Especially not her.</p> <p>But Sparx is determined and strong. Her energy knows no bounds, and soon, the grumpy tiger is smitten by the actress. If only he can find a way to keep her from completing the grueling final test…and from the dangerous bears on the other side of the mountain. Falling in love definitely isn’t the only kind of fall in this mountain adventure.</p> <p><b><i>Mating Cinder</i></b></p> <p>Cinder Brady has big plans. She wants to use her platform as a social media influence to start her own brand of organic cosmetics. Nothing will stand in her way. Not the company that refuses to do business with her until she has a formal education. And definitely not the grumpy and drop-dead-handsome mathematics professor who is hired to teach her private lessons.</p> <p>Professor Forest Cooper might be a jaguar-shifter, but he doesn’t need to find his mate to be happy. All he needs are a few math problems and teaching assistants who don’t cry when he gives orders. But when the dean threatens his tenure if Forest doesn’t lay off the grumpy, he strikes a deal. Tenure in exchange for private lessons for some famous lady. A fair deal until he discovered the maddening woman in the mini-skirt is his mate.</p> <p>The last thing the pair expect during their first lesson is a lion attack. In hiding, Cinder and Forest have to overcome some misconceptions harder to solve than his favorite impossible math problem. Caught up in an international and dangerous scheme, will love be the solution?</p>"; 
